{
  "_about": "Direct RSS/Atom feeds published by Indian newspapers, trade titles and institutions. Each one is a feed the publisher offers to readers, and each item links to that publisher's own article page - which is the point: the openings lane reads the publisher, not an aggregator's redirect. Every entry here was probed once for real; what answered is in config/publisher-feeds.probe.json. An entry in this file is a place to look, not a claim that a requirement exists.",
  "_probed": "2026-09-11. 67 candidate feeds were probed once each by tools/probe-publisher-feeds.mjs --articles; 37 answered with items, a usable publisher article link and a robots.txt that allows both the feed path and that article path, and those 37 are the entries below. The 30 that did not are in config/publisher-feeds.probe.json with the exact reason - 21 never answered 200, 8 answered 200 with a body carrying no RSS <item> and no Atom <entry>, and 1 (Krishak Jagat) serves a working feed whose path its own robots.txt disallows to us.",
